{{define "about.tmpl"}}{{template "layout" .}}
<div class="page-about">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <section>
    <h2>Data sources</h2>
    <p>This application reads three trusted sources and one supplementary set:</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>Quran text (Uthmani)</dt>
      <dd>Tanzil.net Uthmani v1.1, CC-BY-3.0. <a href="https://tanzil.net" rel="noopener">tanzil.net</a></dd>

      <dt>Morphological segmentation</dt>
      <dd>MASAQ (Morphological Analysis of the Standard Arabic Quran). See <code>data/morphology/MASAQ.csv</code>.</dd>

      <dt>Arabic font</dt>
      <dd>Hafs Uthmani font, <code>hafs.woff2</code>.</dd>

      <dt>Root meanings (supplementary)</dt>
      <dd>Generated with AI assistance, stored in <code>meanings-roots-ai.jsonl</code>.
      Provided as a study aid only — not a replacement for classical tafsir.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Architecture</h2>
    <p>Written in Go (vanilla stdlib) and vanilla JS/CSS/HTML. No external frontend frameworks.
    Data is preprocessed once into compact gob files and loaded at startup.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>Quran text: &copy; Tanzil Project, used under CC-BY-3.0. See <a href="https://tanzil.net" rel="noopener">tanzil.net</a> for terms.</p>
    <p>Application code: see <a href="https://github.com/">repository</a> for license.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="about-footer">© {{year}} Quran Reader.</p>
</div>
{{end}}
